{
  "_readme": [
    "TAC-584 behavioural check: the test images and what is really in them.",
    "NO IMAGE IS COMMITTED. This repo is public. Put the files in measurement-runs/media-describe-images/ (gitignored), named as `file` says, or point MEDIA_DESCRIBE_DIR at another folder.",
    "Take them yourself or with the team. No guest's story or photo. People in set E are people who agreed to it.",
    "LABEL BEFORE ANY MODEL CALL. For each image: correct `truth` to what is actually in the photo you took, then set `labelled` to true. `sha256` is filled in by `npm run measure-media-describe -- --hash`, which reads the files and calls no model; it pins the label to the exact file it was written for.",
    "The runner refuses to start, and calls nothing, while any image is missing, unlabelled, or has a hash that does not match its file.",
    "truth.itemsPresent: every menu item really in the picture, in the live menu's own spelling, whether or not it could be told apart. A describe that calls anything else 'unmistakable' is a wrong name.",
    "truth.expectNamed: the items a correct read should name. As the appearance entries stand that is only Pink Panther and Blossom Tonic. Used for the recall report, never for a bar.",
    "truth.isVenue: something IN THE PICTURE ties it to the shop (a distinctive drink, the Parle-G, a branded cup, the room). A plain cortado on a plain table is false even if it was bought there. A visit decided on a false one breaks the bar.",
    "truth.legible: the drinks or food can be made out. Set F is false by design.",
    "The pre-filled truth is what each shot is MEANT to be. It is a starting point for the label, not the label."
  ],
